cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Couret-Unification: Finite Exact Spectral Core on (Z/30Z)× in Lean 4"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as follows."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Couret"
    given-names: "Alexandre"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Rasiguères, France"
abstract: >
  Couret-Unification is a Lean 4 formalization project centered on finite
  spectral and arithmetic structures modulo 30. The frozen layer contains
  0-sorry verified modules, including the finite exact spectral core on
  (Z/30Z)×, character sums, point-defect spectra, G30 triplet classification,
  Cayley-spectrum structures, squarefree-density closures, and related audited
  bridges. Active analytic layers remain explicitly separated and contain
  documented open obligations. No proof of the Riemann Hypothesis is claimed.
  RHClaimed = false.
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - number theory
  - finite spectral model
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - modular arithmetic
  - mod 30
  - Cayley graph
  - CRT
  - Sophie Germain
  - squarefree density
  - finite exact core
version: "v38.5.13"
date-released: "2026-06-21"

